<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rostom of Kartli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1565–1658</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Khosrow Mirza</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rostom, born Khosrow Mirza, was king of Kartli in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> from 1633 to 1658. A Muslim member of the Bagrationi royal house raised at the Safavid court, he was installed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safi-of-persia">Shah Safi</a> and ruled as a loyal Persian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>, bringing Persian customs to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tbilisi">Tbilisi</a> while protecting the Georgian Church. His long reign gave Kartli relative peace after decades of war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rostom-of-kartli.jpg" alt="Rostom of Kartli" width="320" height="531" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Teramo Castelli · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rostom.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
